Write me a python server code, in great detail, that will set up an easy-to-use gambling website.
model
```python
# Import libraries
import random
from flask import Flask, render_template, request

# Create Flask app
app = Flask(__name__)

# Define a list of games
games = ['Rock Paper Scissors', 'Blackjack', 'Pictionary']

# Define the home page
@app.route('/home')
def home():
    return render_template('home.html')

# Define the game page
@app.route('/game')
def game():
    # Select a random game
    game_choice = random.choice(games)
    # Return the game page
    return render_template('game.html', game_choice=game_choice)

# Define the play page
@app.route('/play', methods=['POST'])
def play():
    # Get the user's choice
    choice = request.form['choice']
    # Return the game result
    return render_template('result.html', choice=choice)

# Define the main page
@app.route('/')
def main():
    # Return the main page
    return render_template('main.html')

# Start the Flask server
if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

This code defines a Flask server that sets up a simple gambling website with a home page, a game page, and a play page. The website will allow users to choose a random game and play it.

